RECORD = HEAD ONETREEOFROOTEDATENTITY COLORBELOWITSELFABOVE TWELVEBYTWELVE .

HEAD =
  "// i199.ts — I-199: color is 144 synsets, twelve by twelve"
  "//"
  "// The author, 2026-10-13: the WordNet was a synset-based router, numbers are"
  "// indices, and agents ""can be 144 of any 360 colors""; then, counting, ""138"
  "// synsets under color + 7 is 145, or 144 + 1 globalThis""; and, of Kernighan's"
  "// B ""hello, world"": ""the a b c here is the first 12, the putchar set is the"
  "// second 12, which we refer to as the 11th index"". Found here: in WordNet 3.0"
  "// the synset color (n 04956594) has 138 synsets below it, and its route up to"
  "// entity is 5 more (visual property, property, attribute, abstraction, entity):"
  "// with color itself, 144, each once, none with two parents, and 144 is 12 x 12."
  "// The twelve are a 'hell', b 'o, w', c 'orld', indices 0 to 11: the space 0x20"
  "// at index 6, and the 11th index is the last, 'd'. And 360 hues are 12 sectors"
  "// of 30. The 144 synsets are written here as literals (offset, parent offset,"
  "// first word), read from WordNet 3.0's Prolog files (wn_s.pl, wn_hyp.pl)."
  "import assert from ""node:assert"";"
  "const SYNSETS: [number, number, string][] = ["
